WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:03.650
- [Narrator] Bioluminescence
is the scintillating effect

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:06.070
of a living thing emitting light.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:09.440
And, in a small coastal
town in central Japan,

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.363
one glowing creature is also a delicacy.

00:00:22.569 --> 00:00:25.640
Toyama Bay is around 4,000 feet deep,

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.130
one of the deepest bays in all of Japan

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.700
and home to one of the
only commonly edible

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.003
bioluminescence species in the world.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.580
- [Narrator] Firefly squid fishing

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.350
isn't a normal fishing job.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.403
They have to fish in the dead of night.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.920
Bioluminescence sea creatures

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.580
prefer the dark depths of the ocean.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:01.130
But the firefly squid lights
up the shores when they spawn,

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:02.793
making them easier to catch.

00:01:27.547 --> 00:01:29.770
- [Narrator] Where is
all that squid going?

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.170
Well, to places like Kappo Araki,

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:33.853
a small Japanese restaurant.

00:01:59.339 --> 00:02:01.880
- [Narrator] Chef Araki's menu
includes multiple variants

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.880
of firefly squid: from salted
to grilled, boiled to sashimi.

00:02:08.309 --> 00:02:11.613
All of them delicious, and,
most importantly, fresh.

